━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ InlineVerdicts is Tuple

` What the workers of a round settle about inlining each function, kept once for all of them:
` 0 where it is not settled yet, 1 where it is inlined and 2 where it is not. A verdict hangs on
` the function alone, so workers that settle one at once settle it alike.

+ requests CPointer'Byte
+ readers CPointer'Byte
+ smalls CPointer'Byte

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ IRInliner

` Inlines a function's callees into its IR. A run logs what it asks of the program beyond the
` IR: each function a symbol named (`consulted`), each witness slot it looked up with what it
` found, and whether it fused a reader, which a later round compares to reuse the function.
` `splice-lists` are the lists of the splices it copies with, the first `open-splices` taken.

+ consulted [FunctionId]
+ slot-symbols [StringId]
+ slot-offsets [U32]
+ slot-targets [FunctionId]
+ fused Bool
_ consult-marks [U32]
_ consult-stamp U32
_ tables ProgramTables
_ program Program
_ instances Instances
_ facts Facts
_ types Types
_ bindings Bindings
_ output IRFunction
_ stock-storage Arena
_ stocker-storage Arena
_ stocker Emitter
_ stock [IRFunction]
_ slots [U32]
_ fuser-storages [Arena]
_ fusers [Emitter]
_ symbol-functions [U32]
_ active [FunctionId]
_ expanded-loads [ValueId]
_ verdicts InlineVerdicts
_ levels [Level]
_ fusions [Fused]
_ splice-lists [SpliceLists]
_ open-splices U32
_ traced-level U32
_ traced-row ValueId = 0
_ grew Bool
_ first-round Bool
_ expanding Bool
_ wrapped Bool
_ expanded Bool
_ spare IRFunction

────────────────────
+ This
    - tables ProgramTables
    - program Program
    - instances Instances
    - facts Facts
    - types Types
    - bindings Bindings
    - verdicts InlineVerdicts
    - storage Arena

.. output = IRFunction(storage)
.. spare = IRFunction(storage)
.. stock-storage = Arena()
.. stocker-storage = Arena()
.. stocker = Emitter(tables, program, instances, facts, types, bindings, stocker-storage)

────────────────────
+ do release

stocker.release()
stocker-storage.release()
stock-storage.release()
for fuser in fusers
    fuser.release()
for storage in fuser-storages
    storage.release()

────────────────────
+ do want-type-constants

for type in stocker.type-values
    tables.want-type-constant(type)
for fuser in fusers
    for type in fuser.type-values
        tables.want-type-constant(type)

────────────────────
+ do run IRFunction
    - source IRFunction

consulted.clear()
open-splices = 0
slot-symbols.clear()
slot-offsets.clear()
slot-targets.clear()
fused = false
consult-stamp += 1
. built = source
expanded = false
for round in 0 .. < inline-rounds
    first-round = round == 0
    levels.clear()
    fusions.clear()
    expanding = false
    if built.streams.length != 0
        levels += Level(built, U32.max)
        plan(0)
    for found in levels
        prune(found)
    grew = false
    if fusions.length != 0 || expanding || wants(built) || forwards-any(built)
        built = rebuild(built)
    if !devirtualize(built) && !grew
        = built
= built

────────────────────
_ do rebuild IRFunction
    - source IRFunction

. next = spare
spare = output
output = next
output.reset(source.function)
output.arguments = source.arguments
output.returns = source.returns
output.signals = source.signals
for local in source.locals
    output.locals.append(local)
for number in source.numbers
    output.numbers.append(number)
for constant in source.constants
    output.adopt-constant(constant)
for dependency in source.dependencies
    output.depend(dependency.kind, dependency.symbol, dependency.flags)
. mark = open-splices
. top = open-splice(source)
if levels.length != 0
    top.level = 0
for _ in 0 .. < source.blocks.length
    . block = output.reserve-block()
    top.heads += block
    top.tails += block
active.clear()
active += source.function
expanded-loads.clear()
copy-blocks(top)
open-splices = mark
= output

────────────────────
_ do open-splice Splice
    - source IRFunction

` A splice of `source`, with the next set of `splice-lists`, emptied. Whoever takes one puts
` `open-splices` back once it is done with it.
if open-splices == splice-lists.length
    splice-lists += SpliceLists()
. lists = splice-lists[open-splices]
open-splices += 1
lists.empty()
= Splice(source, lists)

────────────────────
_ do devirtualize Bool
    - ir IRFunction

. resolved = false
for id in 0 .. < ir.instructions.length
    . row = ir.instructions[id]
    if not-call || (row.aux /and/ callee-kind-mask) != CalleeKind.callee-value
        continue
    .. not-call = row.op != .op-call && row.op != .op-call-void
    . target = slot-target(ir, ir.operands[row.operands.start])
    if target == no-function
        continue
    ir.operands.data[row.operands.start] = make-operand
        - .operand-symbol
        - tables.functions[target].symbol
    ir.instructions[id].aux = row.aux - CalleeKind.callee-value
    ir.depend
        - .callee-function
        - target
        - if tables.functions[target].may-panic then may-panic-dependency else 0
    resolved = true
= resolved

────────────────────
_ do slot-target FunctionId
    - ir IRFunction
    - operand Operand

if operand-kind(operand) != .operand-value
    = no-function
. method = ir.instructions[operand-payload(operand)]
if method.op != .op-load || method.layout != pointer-layout
    = no-function
. table = ir.operands[method.operands.start]
. symbol = operand-payload(table)
if operand-kind(table) == .operand-value
    . load = ir.instructions[operand-payload(table)]
    if load.op == .op-frame
        = closure-target(ir, table, method.aux /and/ 0x7fffffff)
    . field = tables.layouts.field(tables.layouts.interface-layout, 1).offset
    if load.op != .op-load || (load.aux /and/ 0x7fffffff) != field
        = no-function
    symbol = field-symbol(ir, ir.operands[load.operands.start], field, 0)
else if operand-kind(table) != .operand-symbol
    = no-function
if symbol == U32.max
    = no-function
. offset = method.aux /and/ 0x7fffffff
. target = tables.witness-slot-function(symbol, offset)
slot-symbols += symbol
slot-offsets += offset
slot-targets += target
if target != no-function
    consult(target)
= target

────────────────────
_ closure-target FunctionId
    - ir IRFunction
    - frame Operand
    - offset U32

|? ir.instructions[operand-payload(frame)].layout != tables.layouts.function-layout || offset != 0
    no-function
|? symbol == U32.max
    no-function
??
    function-of(symbol)

.. symbol = field-symbol(ir, frame, offset, 0)

────────────────────
_ do field-symbol U32
    - ir IRFunction
    - operand Operand
    - offset U32
    - depth U32

if depth > 8 || operand-kind(operand) != .operand-value
    = U32.max
. place = ir.instructions[operand-payload(operand)]
if place.op != .op-frame && place.op != .op-local-address
    = U32.max
. found = U32.max
. writes U32
for id in 0 .. < ir.instructions.length
    . row = ir.instructions[id]
    if row.operands.count == 0
        continue
    . target = ir.operands[row.operands.start]
    if !same-place(ir, target, operand, place)
        continue
    if row.op == .op-copy
        writes += 1
        found = field-symbol(ir, ir.operands[row.operands.start + 1], offset, depth + 1)
    else if row.op == .op-store
        . stored = ir.operands[row.operands.start + 1]
        if (row.aux /and/ 0x7fffffff) == offset
            writes += 1
            found = if is-symbol then operand-payload(stored) else U32.max
            .. is-symbol = operand-kind(stored) == .operand-symbol
    else if row.op == .op-zero || row.op == .op-address
        = U32.max
= if writes == 1 then found else U32.max

────────────────────
_ same-place Bool
    - ir IRFunction
    - target Operand
    - operand Operand
    - place IRInstruction

target == operand || (place.op == .op-local-address && operand-kind(target) == .operand-value && ir.instructions[operand-payload(target)].op == .op-local-address && ir.instructions[operand-payload(target)].aux == place.aux)

────────────────────
_ do wants Bool
    - source IRFunction

. block = no-block
. warm = true
. small = false
for id in 0 .. < source.instructions.length
    . row = source.instructions[id]
    if row.block != block
        if small && warm
            = true
        block = row.block
        warm = true
        small = false
    if first-round && sets-panic(source, row)
        warm = false
    if is-call && (row.aux /and/ callee-kind-mask) == CalleeKind.callee-function
        . target = source.operands[row.operands.start]
        if operand-kind(target) == .operand-symbol
            . position = function-of(operand-payload(target))
            if position == no-function
                continue
            if requested(position) || reads-tuple(position)
                = true
            if first-round && !small && is-small(position)
                small = true
    .. is-call = row.op == .op-call || row.op == .op-call-void
= small && warm

────────────────────
_ do forwards-any Bool
    - source IRFunction

if source.streams.length != 0
    = false
for found in forwarded(source)
    if found != 0
        = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do forwarded [Operand]
    - ir IRFunction

` The argument each frame stands for that the function fills once, whole, from a struct
` argument it never writes, and afterwards only reads: the frame is read as the argument, which
` the caller gave as a copy of its own. A frame or argument whose address reaches anything but a
` read is written. A function that yields keeps its frames, and one given no struct has none.
. found [Operand]
. takes-struct = false
for position in 0 .. < ir.arguments.length
    if tables.layouts.is-struct(ir.arguments[position])
        takes-struct = true
if !takes-struct
    = found
. count = ir.instructions.length
found = Operand[count]
. states = Byte[count]
. written = Bool[ir.arguments.length]
for id in 0 .. < count
    . row = ir.instructions[id]
    if row.op == .op-yield
        for position in 0 .. < count
            found[position] = 0
        = found
    if row.op == .op-address
        continue
    for position in row.operands.start .. < row.operands.end
        . operand = ir.operands[position]
        . root = root-of(ir, operand)
        . index = position - row.operands.start
        . is-argument = operand-kind(root) == .operand-argument
        . is-frame = is-value && ir.instructions[operand-payload(root)].op == .op-frame
            .. is-value = operand-kind(root) == .operand-value
        if !is-argument && !is-frame
            continue
        if reads(ir, row, index, operand)
            continue
        if is-argument
            written[operand-payload(root)] = true
            continue
        . frame = operand-payload(root)
        if operand == root && row.op == .op-copy && index == 0 && states[frame] == 0 && fills-frame
            states[frame] = 1
            found[frame] = ir.operands[row.operands.start + 1]
        else
            states[frame] = 2
        .. fills-frame = fills(ir, row, frame)
for id in 0 .. < count
    if states[id] != 1 || written[operand-payload(found[id])]
        found[id] = 0
= found

────────────────────
_ do root-of Operand
    - ir IRFunction
    - operand Operand

. current = operand
while operand-kind(current) == .operand-value && ir.instructions[operand-payload(current)].op == .op-address
    current = ir.operands[ir.instructions[operand-payload(current)].operands.start]
= current

────────────────────
_ reads Bool
    - ir IRFunction
    - row IRInstruction
    - index U32
    - operand Operand

|? row.op == .op-copy
    index == 1
|? row.op == .op-load
    index == 0
|? row.op == .op-return || row.op == .op-call || row.op == .op-call-void
    (index != 0 || row.op == .op-return) && tables.layouts.is-struct(ir.operand-layout(operand))
??
    false

────────────────────
_ fills Bool
    - ir IRFunction
    - row IRInstruction
    - frame ValueId

|? (row.aux /and/ managed-store-flag) != 0 || operand-kind(source) != .operand-argument
    false
??
    layout == frame-layout && layout == ir.arguments[operand-payload(source)] as LayoutId

.. source = ir.operands[row.operands.start + 1]
.. layout = (row.aux /and/ 0x7fffffff) as LayoutId
.. frame-layout = ir.instructions[frame].layout

────────────────────
_ is-forwarded Bool
    - splice Splice
    - row IRInstruction
    - id ValueId

` Whether a row is a frame read as an argument, or the copy that filled it, which are not
` made again.
|? row.op == .op-frame
    splice.forwards[id] != 0
|? row.op != .op-copy
    false
??
    operand-kind(target) == .operand-value && splice.forwards[operand-payload(target)] != 0

.. target = splice.source.operands[row.operands.start]

────────────────────
_ do inline-callee FunctionId
    - splice Splice
    - row IRInstruction

if row.op != .op-call && row.op != .op-call-void
    = no-function
. kind = row.aux /and/ callee-kind-mask
if kind != CalleeKind.callee-function && kind != CalleeKind.callee-value
    = no-function
. target = remap(splice, splice.source.operands[row.operands.start])
if operand-kind(target) != .operand-symbol
    = no-function
. position = function-of(operand-payload(target))
if position == no-function || is-maker(position) || splice.small
    = no-function
if !requested(position) && !reads-tuple(position)
    . line = if splice.inlined then splice.site-line else row.line
    if !first-round || too-deep || line == 0 || !is-warm(splice) || !is-small(position)
        = no-function
    .. too-deep = splice.depth >= small-depth
if !splice.inlined && !expanded && is-closure(position)
    = no-function
= position

────────────────────
_ do is-warm Bool
    - splice Splice

` Whether the block a splice is copying does not set a panic: a small function is not inlined
` where a panic is made.
. source = splice.source
if splice.warm.length == 0
    splice.warm = Byte[source.blocks.length]
. known = splice.warm[splice.block]
if known != 0
    = known == 1
. rows = source.blocks[splice.block].instructions
. verdict Byte = 1
for id in rows.start .. < rows.end
    if sets-panic(source, source.instructions[id])
        verdict = 2
splice.warm[splice.block] = verdict
= verdict == 1

────────────────────
_ sets-panic Bool
    - ir IRFunction
    - row IRInstruction

row.op == .op-call-void && (callee == panic-set || calls(callee, tables.message-raiser) || calls(callee, tables.panic-raiser))

.. callee = ir.operands[row.operands.start]
.. panic-set = make-operand(.operand-symbol, tables.runtime-symbol(.runtime-panic-set))

────────────────────
_ calls Bool
    - callee Operand
    - raiser FunctionId

raiser != no-function && callee == make-operand(.operand-symbol, tables.functions[raiser].symbol)

────────────────────
_ do function-of FunctionId
    - symbol U32

if symbol-functions.length == 0
    for _ in 0 .. < tables.bundle.string-count
        symbol-functions += no-function
    for position in 0 .. < tables.functions.length
        . named = tables.functions[position].symbol
        if named < symbol-functions.length
            symbol-functions[named] = position as U32
if symbol >= symbol-functions.length
    = no-function
. found = symbol-functions[symbol]
if found != no-function
    consult(found)
= found

────────────────────
_ do consult
    - position FunctionId

if consult-marks.length == 0
    consult-marks = U32[tables.functions.length]
if consult-marks[position] != consult-stamp
    consult-marks[position] = consult-stamp
    consulted += position

────────────────────
_ do requested Bool
    - position FunctionId

` Whether a function is inlined wherever it is called, settled once for the round.
. known = verdicts.requests[position]
if known != 0
    = known == 1
. asked = asks-for(position)
verdicts.requests[position] = if asked then 1 else 2
= asked

────────────────────
_ do asks-for Bool
    - position FunctionId

. function = tables.functions[position]
if function.kind == .adapter || function.kind == .witness
    = true
if function.kind == .union-dispatch
    = forwards-getter(function.place)
if function.kind != .instance-body || function.instance == no-instance || recursive
    = false
.. recursive = tables.is-recursive(function.instance)
. row = instances.rows[function.instance]
match? program.modules[row.module].decls[row.decl]
    | .decl-function(fn)
        if pipeline-or-feed || fn.kind == .closure-decl || fn.kind == .iterator-decl
            = true
        .. pipeline-or-feed = fn.kind == .pipeline-decl || fn.kind == .feed-decl
= tables.asks-inline(function.instance)

────────────────────
_ do reads-tuple Bool
    - position FunctionId

` Whether a function is one the reference inlines wherever it is called, though it asks for
` nothing: it reads one small tuple of numbers, gives a number, and cannot panic. Its body is
` emitted where it is first asked about, so that the answer does not hang on what was inlined
` before.
. known = verdicts.readers[position]
if known != 0
    = known == 1
. fits = signs-reader(position) && emits-reader(position)
verdicts.readers[position] = if fits then 1 else 2
= fits

────────────────────
_ do emits-reader Bool
    - position FunctionId

. found = emitted(position)
if !found
    = false
= reads-only(found)

────────────────────
_ signs-reader Bool
    - position FunctionId

|? function.kind != .instance-body || function.instance == no-instance
    false
|? row.may-panic || row.is-generator || tables.is-recursive(instance)
    false
|? signature.args.count != 1 || signature.errors.count != 0 || signature.returns == no-type
    false
|? !intrinsic-is-numeric(returned) || returned == .cpointer
    false
??
    is-small-tuple(instances.argument-type(instance, 0))

.. function = tables.functions[position]
.. instance = function.instance
.. row = instances.rows[instance]
.. signature = instances.signatures[instance]
.. returned = types.intrinsic-of(signature.returns)

────────────────────
_ do is-small Bool
    - position FunctionId

` Whether a function no one asked to inline is inlined where it is called, as one too small
` to be worth a call: a plain function, getter, setter or constructor of a few lines that
` cannot panic or raise an error, so that no stack trace has its frame, does not yield and is
` not recursive. Its body is emitted where it is first asked about, so that the answer does
` not hang on what was inlined before.
. known = verdicts.smalls[position]
if known != 0
    = known == 1
. function = tables.functions[position]
. fits = function.kind == .instance-body && function.instance != no-instance && !recursive
    .. recursive = tables.is-recursive(function.instance)
if fits
    . row = instances.rows[function.instance]
    fits = uninterrupted && infallible && is-plain(row) && emits-small(position)
    .. uninterrupted = !row.may-panic && !row.is-generator
    .. infallible = instances.signatures[function.instance].errors.count == 0
verdicts.smalls[position] = if fits then 1 else 2
= fits

────────────────────
_ do emits-small Bool
    - position FunctionId

. found = emitted(position)
if !found
    = false
. ir = found
= !ir.signals && ir.instructions.length <= small-size && ir.streams.length == 0 && !expands-any(ir)

────────────────────
_ do is-plain Bool
    - row Instance

. tree = program.modules[row.module].tree
match? program.modules[row.module].decls[row.decl]
    | .decl-function(fn)
        if fn.kind != .function-decl && not-accessor && not-constructor
            = false
        .. not-accessor = fn.kind != .getter-decl && fn.kind != .setter-decl
        .. not-constructor = fn.kind != .constructor-decl && fn.kind != .tuple-constructor-decl
        match? tree.nodes[fn.syntax]
            | .node-function-syntax(syntax)
                if syntax.body == 0
                    = false
                . loc = tree.nodes[syntax.body].loc
                = loc.end.line - loc.begin.line < small-lines
= false

────────────────────
_ do is-small-tuple Bool
    - type TypeId

` Whether a value is a tuple whose few fields are numbers or such tuples, held with no managed
` pointer: one a reader can read where its caller holds it.
if type == no-type || types.intrinsic-of(type) != .tuple
    = false
. layout = tables.layouts.values[type]
if layout == no-layout || !tables.layouts.is-struct(layout)
    = false
. row = tables.layouts.rows[layout]
if row.is-managed || row.fields.count > reader-fields
    = false
for index in 0 .. < row.fields.count
    . field = tables.layouts.field(layout, index)
    if tables.layouts.is-struct(field.layout) && !is-small-tuple(field.type)
        = false
= true

────────────────────
_ do reads-only Bool
    - inlined IRFunction

` Whether a body only reads the tuple it is given: one block of loads from it, and of what
` is computed from them, that ends in the return of a number.
if inlined.signals || inlined.order.length != 1 || inlined.instructions.length > reader-size
    = false
for made in inlined.instructions
    . op = made.op
    if op == .op-load || op == .op-address
        if !reads-argument(inlined, inlined.operands[made.operands.start])
            = false
    else if op == .op-return
        if made.aux != ReturnKind.return-normal
            = false
    else if op != .op-arithmetic && op != .op-bitwise && op != .op-num-cast && op != .op-negate && op != .op-bitwise-not && op != .op-compare && op != .op-count-leading-zeros && op != .op-float-math
        = false
= true

────────────────────
_ reads-argument Bool
    - inlined IRFunction
    - operand Operand

|? kind == .operand-argument
    true
|? kind != .operand-value
    false
??
    row.op == .op-address && reads-argument(inlined, inlined.operands[row.operands.start])

.. kind = operand-kind(operand)
.. row = inlined.instructions[operand-payload(operand)]

────────────────────
_ falls-back Bool
    - position FunctionId

has-instance && tables.is-recursive(function.instance) && tables.asks-inline(function.instance)

.. function = tables.functions[position]
.. has-instance = function.kind == .instance-body && function.instance != no-instance

────────────────────
_ do forwards-getter Bool
    - place U32

. forward = facts.forwards[place]
if forward.given != 0
    = false
match? program.modules[instances.rows[forward.instance].module].tree.nodes[forward.syntax]
    | .node-get-expression(read)
        . kind = types.intrinsic-of(facts.node-type(forward.instance, read.object))
        = kind != .table-row && kind != .immutable-table-row
= false

────────────────────
_ do is-closure Bool
    - position FunctionId

. function = tables.functions[position]
if function.kind != .instance-body || function.instance == no-instance
    = false
. row = instances.rows[function.instance]
match? program.modules[row.module].decls[row.decl]
    | .decl-function(fn)
        if fn.kind != .closure-decl
            = false
        match? program.modules[row.module].tree.nodes[fn.syntax]
            | .node-function-syntax(syntax)
                = !syntax.is-inline
        = true
= false

────────────────────
_ is-maker Bool
    - position FunctionId

|? position == no-function
    false
|? function.kind != .instance-body || function.instance == no-instance
    false
??
    tables.step-functions[function.instance] != no-function && requested(position)

.. function = tables.functions[position]

────────────────────
_ do emitted IRFunction?
    - position FunctionId

` A function's IR as it is inlined, emitted once for the round into the stock, which nothing
` writes after, however many sites take it: null where it is refused or bridged.
if slots.length == 0
    slots = U32[tables.functions.length]
. slot = slots[position]
if slot == U32.max
    = null
if slot != 0
    = stock[slot - 1]
stocker-storage.reset()
stocker.ir = IRFunction(stock-storage)
stocker.emit(position)
if stocker.is-refused || stocker.bridged
    slots[position] = U32.max
    = null
stock += stocker.ir
slots[position] = stock.length as U32
= stocker.ir

────────────────────
_ do fuser-at Emitter
    - index U32

while fusers.length <= index
    . made = Arena()
    fuser-storages += made
    fusers += Emitter(tables, program, instances, facts, types, bindings, made)
= fusers[index]

────────────────────
_ home ModuleId
    - position FunctionId

if function.site-module == U32.max then function.module else function.site-module

.. function = tables.functions[position]

────────────────────
_ mark U32
    - kind U32
    - index U32

(kind /lshift/ mark-shift) /or/ index

────────────────────
_ do plan
    - level U32

. ir = levels[level].ir
for stream in 0 .. < ir.streams.length
    . found = ir.streams[stream]
    . known = found.begin != U32.max && found.read != U32.max && found.done != no-block
    for position in 0 .. < found.ends.length
        if found.ends[position] == U32.max
            known = false
    wrapped = false
    if !known || !trace(level, found.made, stream as U32)
        if wrapped
            keep-protocol(levels[level], found)
        continue
    . owner = traced-level
    . row = traced-row
    if !once(level, found.begin, owner, row)
        continue
    . owned = levels[owner].ir
    . maker = function-of(operand-payload(owned.operands[owned.instructions[row].operands.start]))
    if nests(level, maker)
        continue
    . index = fusions.length
    . fuser = fuser-at(index as U32)
    fuser-storages[index].reset()
    fused = true
    fuser.emit-fused(maker, ir.instructions[found.read].layout)
    if fuser.is-refused
        continue
    . fused = Fused(fuser.ir, maker, owner, row, level, stream as U32)
    if !admits(fused)
        continue
    fused.level = levels.length as U32
    fusions += fused
    levels += Level(fused.ir, index as U32)
    levels[owner].marks[row] = mark(mark-absorb, index as U32)
    levels[level].marks[found.begin] = mark(mark-begin, index as U32)
    levels[level].marks[found.read] = mark(mark-read, index as U32)
    for position in 0 .. < found.ends.length
        levels[level].marks[found.ends[position]] = mark(mark-end, index as U32)
    if found.head != no-block && found.polled != found.head
        levels[level].skips[found.head] = found.polled
    plan(fused.level)

────────────────────
_ do keep-protocol
    - found Level
    - traced IRStream

. rows [ValueId]
rows += traced.begin
rows += traced.read
for position in 0 .. < traced.ends.length
    rows += traced.ends[position]
for row in rows
    if found.marks[row] == 0
        found.marks[row] = mark(mark-keep, 0)

────────────────────
_ do prune
    - found Level

. pending [ValueId]
for id in 0 .. < found.ir.instructions.length
    . kind = found.marks[id] /zrshift/ mark-shift
    if kind == mark-begin || kind == mark-read || kind == mark-end
        pending += id as ValueId
release(found, pending, found.dead)

────────────────────
_ do release
    - found Level
    - pending [ValueId]
    - dead [Bool]

. ir = found.ir
. left [U32]
for count in found.uses
    left += count
while pending.length != 0
    . id = pending[pending.length - 1]
    pending.pop()
    . row = ir.instructions[id]
    for position in row.operands.start .. < row.operands.end
        . operand = ir.operands[position]
        if operand-kind(operand) == .operand-value
            . used = operand-payload(operand)
            left[used] -= 1
            if left[used] == 0 && is-pure(ir.instructions[used].op)
                dead[used] = true
                pending += used

────────────────────
_ is-pure Bool
    - op IROp

match op
    |= .op-load
        true
    |= .op-address
        true
    |= .op-local-address
        true
    |= .op-load-local
        true
    |= .op-frame
        true
    |= .op-num-cast
        true
    |= .op-arithmetic
        true
    |= .op-bitwise
        true
    |= .op-compare
        true
    |= .op-negate
        true
    |= .op-bitwise-not
        true
    |= .op-inlined-name
        true
    ??
        false

────────────────────
_ do nests Bool
    - level U32
    - maker FunctionId

. current = level
while levels[current].fused != U32.max
    . fused = fusions[levels[current].fused]
    if fused.maker == maker
        = true
    current = fused.consumer
= levels[current].ir.function == maker

────────────────────
_ do once Bool
    - level U32
    - begin ValueId
    - owner U32
    - row ValueId

. current = level
. start = begin
while current != owner
    . ir = levels[current].ir
    if repeats(ir, ir.instructions[start].block, no-block)
        = false
    . fused = fusions[levels[current].fused]
    current = fused.consumer
    start = levels[current].ir.streams[fused.stream].begin
. ir = levels[owner].ir
= !repeats(ir, ir.instructions[start].block, ir.instructions[row].block)

────────────────────
_ do repeats Bool
    - ir IRFunction
    - block IRBlockId
    - boundary IRBlockId

. seen [Bool]
for _ in 0 .. < ir.blocks.length
    seen += false
. pending [IRBlockId]
block-successors(ir, block, pending, true)
while pending.length != 0
    . next = pending[pending.length - 1]
    pending.pop()
    if next == boundary || seen[next]
        continue
    if next == block
        = true
    seen[next] = true
    block-successors(ir, next, pending, true)
= false

────────────────────
_ do trace Bool
    - level U32
    - operand Operand
    - stream U32 = U32.max

. found = levels[level]
. ir = found.ir
. payload = operand-payload(operand)
if operand-kind(operand) == .operand-argument
    if found.fused == U32.max || argument-uses(ir, payload) != 1
        = false
    . fused = fusions[found.fused]
    . owned = levels[fused.owner].ir
    = trace(fused.owner, owned.operands[owned.instructions[fused.row].operands.start + 1 + payload])
if operand-kind(operand) != .operand-value
    = false
. row = ir.instructions[payload]
if row.op == .op-call
    if found.uses[payload] != 1 || (row.aux /and/ callee-kind-mask) != CalleeKind.callee-function
        = false
    . target = ir.operands[row.operands.start]
    if operand-kind(target) != .operand-symbol
        = false
    . position = function-of(operand-payload(target))
    if !is-maker(position)
        if found.marks[payload] == 0 && wraps-maker(position)
            found.marks[payload] = mark(mark-expand, 0)
            expanding = true
            wrapped = true
        = false
    traced-level = level
    traced-row = payload
    = true
if row.op == .op-frame
    = trace-frame(level, payload)
if row.op == .op-local-address || row.op == .op-load-local
    . held = local-source(level, row.aux, stream)
    = held != 0 && trace(level, held)
= false

────────────────────
_ do wraps-maker Bool
    - position FunctionId

if position == no-function || tables.functions[position].kind != .instance-body
    = false
. found = emitted(position)
if !found
    = false
. ir = found
. returned Operand = 0
. returns U32
for row in ir.instructions
    if row.op == .op-return && row.aux != ReturnKind.return-panic
        returns += 1
        returned = if row.operands.count != 0 then ir.operands[row.operands.start] else 0
if returns != 1 || operand-kind(returned) != .operand-value
    = false
. call = ir.instructions[operand-payload(returned)]
if call.op != .op-call || (call.aux /and/ callee-kind-mask) != CalleeKind.callee-function
    = false
. target = ir.operands[call.operands.start]
= operand-kind(target) == .operand-symbol && is-maker(function-of(operand-payload(target)))

────────────────────
_ do trace-frame Bool
    - level U32
    - frame ValueId

. found = levels[level]
. ir = found.ir
. copied Operand = 0
. copies U32
. boxed Operand = 0
. tagged = false
. stores U32
for id in 0 .. < ir.instructions.length
    . row = ir.instructions[id]
    if row.operands.count == 0 || ir.operands[row.operands.start] != frame-operand
        continue
    .. frame-operand = make-operand(.operand-value, frame)
    if row.op == .op-copy
        copies += 1
        copied = ir.operands[row.operands.start + 1]
    else if row.op == .op-store
        stores += 1
        . stored = ir.operands[row.operands.start + 1]
        . offset = row.aux /and/ 0x7fffffff
        if offset == 0
            boxed = stored
        else if offset == managed-size && operand-kind(stored) == .operand-symbol
            tagged = true
        .. managed-size = tables.layouts.rows[managed-layout].size
    else if row.op == .op-zero || row.op == .op-address
        = false
if copies == 1 && stores == 0 && found.uses[frame] == 2
    = trace(level, copied)
if copies != 0 || stores != 2 || !tagged || other-uses || operand-kind(boxed) != .operand-value
    = false
.. other-uses = found.uses[frame] != 3
. box = operand-payload(boxed)
. allocation = ir.instructions[box]
if allocation.op != .op-call || not-runtime || found.uses[box] != 2
    = false
.. not-runtime = (allocation.aux /and/ callee-kind-mask) != CalleeKind.callee-runtime
if ir.operands[allocation.operands.start] != allocator
    = false
.. allocator = make-operand(.operand-symbol, tables.runtime-symbol(.runtime-allocate-object))
. inner Operand = 0
. fills U32
for id in 0 .. < ir.instructions.length
    . row = ir.instructions[id]
    if row.op == .op-copy && ir.operands[row.operands.start] == boxed
        fills += 1
        inner = ir.operands[row.operands.start + 1]
= fills == 1 && trace(level, inner)

────────────────────
_ do local-source Operand
    - level U32
    - local LocalId
    - stream U32

. found = levels[level]
. ir = found.ir
. absorbed [Bool]
for _ in 0 .. < ir.instructions.length
    absorbed += false
if stream != U32.max
    absorb-protocol(found, ir.streams[stream], absorbed)
. source Operand = 0
. writes U32
. reads U32
for id in 0 .. < ir.instructions.length
    . row = ir.instructions[id]
    if row.op == .op-store-local && row.aux == local
        writes += 1
        source = ir.operands[row.operands.start]
    else if row.op == .op-load-local && row.aux == local
        reads += 1
    else if row.op == .op-local-address && row.aux == local && !absorbed[id]
        if found.uses[id] > 1
            = 0
        if found.uses[id] == 1
            reads += 1
    else if (row.op == .op-copy || row.op == .op-zero) && row.operands.count != 0
        . target = ir.operands[row.operands.start]
        if operand-kind(target) == .operand-value
            . held = ir.instructions[operand-payload(target)]
            if held.op == .op-local-address && held.aux == local
                writes += 1
                reads -= 1
                source = if row.op == .op-zero then 0 else ir.operands[row.operands.start + 1]
= if writes == 1 && reads <= 1 then source else 0

────────────────────
_ do absorb-protocol
    - found Level
    - traced IRStream
    - absorbed [Bool]

. pending [ValueId]
pending += traced.begin
pending += traced.read
for position in 0 .. < traced.ends.length
    pending += traced.ends[position]
release(found, pending, absorbed)

────────────────────
_ do argument-uses U32
    - ir IRFunction
    - argument U32

. count U32
for position in 0 .. < ir.operands.length
    if ir.operands[position] == make-operand(.operand-argument, argument)
        count += 1
= count

────────────────────
_ do admits Bool
    - fused Fused

. produced = fused.ir
. consumer = levels[fused.consumer].ir
. found = consumer.streams[fused.stream]
. read = consumer.instructions[found.read]
. owned = levels[fused.owner].ir
. call = owned.instructions[fused.row]
. checked = (call.aux /and/ checked-call-flag) != 0
. given = call.operands.count - 1 - (if checked then 1u32 else 0u32)
if produced.order.length == 0 || produced.arguments.length != given || read.layout == void-layout
    = false
for _ in 0 .. < produced.blocks.length
    fused.closing += false
    fused.body += false
for id in 0 .. < produced.instructions.length
    . row = produced.instructions[id]
    for position in row.operands.start .. < row.operands.end
        if operand-kind(produced.operands[position]) == .operand-environment
            = false
    if row.op == .op-yield
        if produced.operand-layout(produced.operands[row.operands.start]) != read.layout
            = false
        fused.yields += id as ValueId
        if row.aux != no-block
            fused.closes = true
            mark-closing(fused, row.aux)
mark-body(fused)
. live [ValueId]
for yielded in fused.yields
    if fused.body[produced.instructions[yielded].block]
        live += yielded
fused.yields = live
if fused.closes && found.ends.length == 0
    = false
. outer = levels[fused.consumer].fused
if outer != U32.max
    . around = fusions[outer]
    . begun = consumer.instructions[found.begin].block
    if around.closing[begun] || !around.body[begun]
        = false
    for position in 0 .. < found.ends.length
        . ended = consumer.instructions[found.ends[position]].block
        if !around.closing[ended] && !around.body[ended]
            = false
for id in 0 .. < produced.instructions.length
    . row = produced.instructions[id]
    if returns-error && (fused.closing[row.block] || !tables.layouts.is-struct(read.layout))
        = false
    .. returns-error = row.op == .op-return && row.aux == ReturnKind.return-error
    if row.op == .op-return && row.aux == ReturnKind.return-panic
        if fused.closing[row.block]
            for position in 0 .. < found.ends.length
                if (consumer.instructions[found.ends[position]].aux /and/ checked-call-flag) == 0
                    = false
        if fused.body[row.block] && (read.aux /and/ checked-call-flag) == 0
            = false
    if fused.closing[row.block] && fused.body[row.block] && is-call && calls-function
        = false
    .. is-call = row.op == .op-call || row.op == .op-call-void
    .. calls-function = (row.aux /and/ callee-kind-mask) == CalleeKind.callee-function
for stream in 0 .. < produced.streams.length
    . inner = produced.streams[stream]
    for position in 0 .. < inner.ends.length
        . ended = produced.instructions[inner.ends[position]].block
        if fused.closing[ended] && fused.body[ended]
            = false
= find-crossings(fused)

────────────────────
_ do find-crossings Bool
    - fused Fused

. produced = fused.ir
. count = produced.blocks.length
for _ in 0 .. < produced.instructions.length
    fused.crossing += false
. roots [IRBlockId]
roots += produced.order[0]
for yielded in fused.yields
    . row = produced.instructions[yielded]
    roots += operand-payload(produced.operands[row.operands.start + 1])
    if row.aux != no-block
        roots += row.aux
. numbers [U32]
. idoms [U32]
for _ in 0 .. < count + 1
    numbers += U32.max
    idoms += U32.max
. sequence [IRBlockId]
. visiting [IRBlockId]
. cursors [U32]
. successors [IRBlockId]
for root in roots
    if numbers[root] != U32.max - 1 && numbers[root] == U32.max
        visiting += root
        cursors += 0
        numbers[root] = U32.max - 1
        while visiting.length != 0
            . top = visiting.length - 1
            . block = visiting[top]
            successors.clear()
            block-successors(produced, block, successors)
            if cursors[top] < successors.length
                . next = successors[cursors[top]]
                cursors[top] += 1
                if numbers[next] == U32.max
                    numbers[next] = U32.max - 1
                    visiting += next
                    cursors += 0
                continue
            sequence += block
            visiting.pop()
            cursors.pop()
for position in 0 .. < sequence.length
    numbers[sequence[position]] = position as U32
numbers[count] = sequence.length as U32
idoms[count] = count as U32
. preds [[IRBlockId]]
for _ in 0 .. < count + 1
    . none [IRBlockId]
    preds += none
for root in roots
    preds[root] += count as IRBlockId
for block in sequence
    successors.clear()
    block-successors(produced, block, successors)
    for next in successors
        preds[next] += block
. changed = true
while changed
    changed = false
    for back in 0 .. < sequence.length
        . block = sequence[sequence.length - 1 - back]
        . chosen = U32.max
        for pred in preds[block]
            if idoms[pred] == U32.max
                continue
            chosen = if chosen == U32.max then pred else meet(pred, chosen, idoms, numbers)
        if chosen != U32.max && idoms[block] != chosen
            idoms[block] = chosen
            changed = true
for id in 0 .. < produced.instructions.length
    . row = produced.instructions[id]
    if idoms[row.block] == U32.max
        continue
    for position in row.operands.start .. < row.operands.end
        . operand = produced.operands[position]
        if operand-kind(operand) != .operand-value
            continue
        . made = operand-payload(operand)
        . home = produced.instructions[made].block
        . user = row.block
        if row.op == .op-phi
            user = operand-payload(produced.operands[position + 1])
        if home == user || dominates(home, user, idoms, count as U32)
            continue
        if row.op == .op-phi || tables.layouts.is-struct(produced.instructions[made].layout)
            = false
        fused.crossing[made] = true
= true

────────────────────
_ do block-successors
    - produced IRFunction
    - block IRBlockId
    - found [IRBlockId]
    - yields Bool = false

. rows = produced.blocks[block].instructions
for id in rows.start .. < rows.end
    . row = produced.instructions[id]
    if row.op == .op-phi || (row.op == .op-yield && !yields)
        continue
    for position in row.operands.start .. < row.operands.end
        . operand = produced.operands[position]
        if operand-kind(operand) == .operand-block
            found += operand-payload(operand)

────────────────────
_ do meet U32
    - left U32
    - right U32
    - idoms [U32]
    - numbers [U32]

. first = left
. second = right
while first != second
    while numbers[first] < numbers[second]
        first = idoms[first]
    while numbers[second] < numbers[first]
        second = idoms[second]
= first

────────────────────
_ do dominates Bool
    - dominator U32
    - block U32
    - idoms [U32]
    - root U32

. current = block
while current != root
    if current == dominator
        = true
    current = idoms[current]
= current == dominator

────────────────────
_ do mark-closing
    - fused Fused
    - head IRBlockId

. produced = fused.ir
. pending [IRBlockId]
pending += head
while pending.length != 0
    . block = pending[pending.length - 1]
    pending.pop()
    if fused.closing[block]
        continue
    fused.closing[block] = true
    . rows = produced.blocks[block].instructions
    for id in rows.start .. < rows.end
        . row = produced.instructions[id]
        if row.op != .op-phi
            for position in row.operands.start .. < row.operands.end
                . operand = produced.operands[position]
                if operand-kind(operand) == .operand-block
                    pending += operand-payload(operand)

────────────────────
_ do mark-body
    - fused Fused

. produced = fused.ir
. pending [IRBlockId]
pending += produced.order[0]
while pending.length != 0
    . block = pending[pending.length - 1]
    pending.pop()
    if fused.body[block]
        continue
    fused.body[block] = true
    . rows = produced.blocks[block].instructions
    for id in rows.start .. < rows.end
        . row = produced.instructions[id]
        if row.op != .op-phi
            for position in row.operands.start .. < row.operands.end
                . operand = produced.operands[position]
                if operand-kind(operand) == .operand-block
                    pending += operand-payload(operand)

────────────────────
_ do region [Bool]
    - produced IRFunction
    - head IRBlockId

. inside [Bool]
for _ in 0 .. < produced.blocks.length
    inside += false
. pending [IRBlockId]
pending += head
while pending.length != 0
    . block = pending[pending.length - 1]
    pending.pop()
    if inside[block]
        continue
    inside[block] = true
    block-successors(produced, block, pending)
= inside

────────────────────
_ do copy-blocks
    - splice Splice

. source = splice.source
if splice.level == U32.max && splice.fused == U32.max
    splice.forwards = forwarded(source)
    for id in 0 .. < splice.forwards.length
        if splice.forwards[id] != 0
            splice.values[id] = remap(splice, splice.forwards[id])
for position in 0 .. < source.order.length
    . block = source.order[position]
    if splice.only.length != 0 && !splice.only[block]
        continue
    output.start-block(splice.heads[block])
    if splice.level != U32.max && levels[splice.level].skips[block] != no-block
        jump(splice.heads[levels[splice.level].skips[block]])
        splice.tails[block] = output.current
        continue
    splice.block = block
    . rows = source.blocks[block].instructions
    for id in rows.start .. < rows.end
        . row = source.instructions[id]
        if splice.forwards.length != 0 && is-forwarded(splice, row, id)
            continue
        if !fuse-row(splice, id, row)
            . callee = inline-callee(splice, row)
            if callee == no-function || !expand(splice, id, row, callee)
                copy-row(splice, id, row)
        if splice.fused != U32.max && fusions[splice.fused].spills[id] != no-local
            store-local(fusions[splice.fused].spills[id], splice.values[id])
    splice.tails[block] = output.current
for patched in splice.phi-values
    output.operands.data[patched] = remap(splice, output.operands[patched])
for patched in splice.phi-blocks
    output.operands.data[patched] = make-operand
        - .operand-block
        - splice.tails[operand-payload(output.operands[patched])]
if !splice.closing
    carry-streams(splice)

────────────────────
_ do carry-streams
    - splice Splice

. source = splice.source
for found in source.streams
    if found.begin == U32.max || found.read == U32.max || found.done == no-block
        continue
    if splice.level != U32.max && (begin-mark /zrshift/ mark-shift) == mark-begin
        continue
    .. begin-mark = levels[splice.level].marks[found.begin]
    . made = carried(splice, found.made)
    . begin = copied(splice, found.begin)
    . read = copied(splice, found.read)
    if made == 0 || begin == U32.max || read == U32.max || !kept(splice, found.done)
        continue
    . ends [ValueId]
    for position in 0 .. < found.ends.length
        . ended = if found.ends[position] != U32.max then copied-end else U32.max
            .. copied-end = copied(splice, found.ends[position])
        if ended != U32.max
            ends += ended
    if ends.length != found.ends.length
        continue
    . head = if keeps-head then splice.heads[found.head] else no-block
        .. keeps-head = found.head != no-block && kept(splice, found.head)
    . polled = if keeps-polled then splice.heads[found.polled] else no-block
        .. keeps-polled = found.polled != no-block && kept(splice, found.polled)
    . stream = output.streams.length
    output.streams.append
        - IRStream(made, begin, read, IdList(), head, polled, splice.heads[found.done])
    for ended in ends
        output.end-stream(stream as U32, ended)

────────────────────
_ do carried Operand
    - splice Splice
    - operand Operand

. payload = operand-payload(operand)
match operand-kind(operand)
    |= .operand-value
        if splice.fused != U32.max && fusions[splice.fused].spills[payload] != no-local
            = 0
        . value = splice.values[payload]
        = if is-value || operand-kind(value) == .operand-argument then value else 0
            .. is-value = operand-kind(value) == .operand-value
    |= .operand-argument
        if !splice.inlined
            = operand
        . value = splice.arguments[payload]
        = if operand-kind(value) == .operand-value || is-argument then value else 0
            .. is-argument = operand-kind(value) == .operand-argument
    ??
        = 0
= 0

────────────────────
_ copied ValueId
    - splice Splice
    - id ValueId

|? operand-kind(value) != .operand-value
    U32.max
|? copy.op != row.op || not-call || copy.operands.count != row.operands.count
    U32.max
??
    made

.. value = splice.values[id]
.. made = operand-payload(value)
.. row = splice.source.instructions[id]
.. copy = output.instructions[made]
.. not-call = copy.op != .op-call && copy.op != .op-call-void

────────────────────
_ kept Bool
    - splice Splice
    - block IRBlockId

splice.only.length == 0 || splice.only[block]

────────────────────
_ do fuse-row Bool
    - splice Splice
    - id ValueId
    - row IRInstruction

if splice.level != U32.max && levels[splice.level].dead[id]
    = true
if splice.fused != U32.max
    if row.op == .op-yield
        fused-yield(splice, id, row)
        = true
    if row.op == .op-return
        fused-return(splice, row)
        = true
    if row.op == .op-load && forward-field(splice, id, row)
        = true
if splice.level == U32.max
    = false
. marked = levels[splice.level].marks[id]
if marked == 0
    = false
. index = marked /and/ ((1u32 /lshift/ mark-shift) - 1)
. kind = marked /zrshift/ mark-shift
if kind == mark-expand
    . callee = function-of(operand-payload(splice.source.operands[row.operands.start]))
    if !expand(splice, id, row, callee)
        copy-row(splice, id, row)
else if kind == mark-keep
    copy-row(splice, id, row)
else if kind == mark-absorb
    absorb(splice, id, row, index)
else if kind == mark-begin
    fuse-begin(splice, id, row, index)
else if kind == mark-read
    fuse-read(splice, id, row, index)
else
    fuse-end(splice, id, row, index)
= true

────────────────────
_ do forward-field Bool
    - splice Splice
    - id ValueId
    - row IRInstruction

. base = splice.source.operands[row.operands.start]
if operand-kind(base) != .operand-argument
    = false
. fused = fusions[splice.fused]
. argument = operand-payload(base)
for position in 0 .. < fused.field-arguments.length
    if fused.field-arguments[position] == argument && same-offset && same-layout
        splice.values[id] = fused.field-values[position]
        = true
    .. same-offset = fused.field-offsets[position] == row.aux
    .. same-layout = fused.field-layouts[position] == row.layout
= false

────────────────────
_ do absorb
    - splice Splice
    - id ValueId
    - row IRInstruction
    - index U32

. fused = fusions[index]
. checked = (row.aux /and/ checked-call-flag) != 0
. last = row.operands.end - (if checked then 1u32 else 0u32)
for position in row.operands.start + 1 .. < last
    . argument = position - row.operands.start - 1
    . operand = remap(splice, splice.source.operands[position])
    . layout = fused.ir.arguments[argument]
    if tables.layouts.is-struct(layout) && tables.layouts.rows[layout].size != 0
        . held = frame(layout)
        copy(held, operand, layout)
        fused.arguments += held
        note-fields(splice, argument, splice.source.operands[position], fused)
    else
        fused.arguments += operand
if row.op == .op-call
    splice.values[id] = blank(row.layout)

────────────────────
_ do note-fields
    - splice Splice
    - argument U32
    - operand Operand
    - fused Fused

. ir = splice.source
. current = operand
while operand-kind(current) == .operand-value && ir.instructions[operand-payload(current)].op == .op-frame
    . copied Operand = 0
    . copies U32
    . stores U32
    for id in 0 .. < ir.instructions.length
        . row = ir.instructions[id]
        if row.operands.count == 0 || ir.operands[row.operands.start] != current
            continue
        if row.op == .op-copy
            copies += 1
            copied = ir.operands[row.operands.start + 1]
        else if row.op == .op-store
            stores += 1
        else if row.op == .op-zero || row.op == .op-address
            =
    if copies == 1 && stores == 0
        current = copied
        continue
    if copies != 0
        =
    . first = fused.field-arguments.length
    for id in 0 .. < ir.instructions.length
        . row = ir.instructions[id]
        if row.op != .op-store || ir.operands[row.operands.start] != current
            continue
        . stored = ir.operands[row.operands.start + 1]
        . offset = row.aux /and/ 0x7fffffff
        . repeated = false
        for position in first .. < fused.field-arguments.length
            if fused.field-offsets[position] == offset
                repeated = true
        if repeated || (operand-kind(stored) == .operand-value && uncopied)
            continue
        .. uncopied = splice.values[operand-payload(stored)] == 0
        fused.field-arguments += argument
        fused.field-offsets += offset
        fused.field-layouts += ir.operand-layout(stored)
        fused.field-values += remap(splice, stored)
    =

────────────────────
_ do fuse-begin
    - splice Splice
    - id ValueId
    - row IRInstruction
    - index U32

. fused = fusions[index]
. consumer = splice.source
. found = consumer.streams[fused.stream]
. read = consumer.instructions[found.read]
grew = true
if row.op == .op-call
    splice.values[id] = blank(row.layout)
if tables.layouts.is-struct(read.layout)
    fused.result = frame(read.layout)
else
    fused.held = output.add-local(read.layout)
if fused.closes || fused.yields.length > 1
    fused.state = output.add-local(u32-layout)
    store-local(fused.state, number(.machine-u32, 0))
fused.after-read = output.reserve-block()
fused.exhausted = splice.heads[found.done]
if (read.aux /and/ checked-call-flag) != 0
    fused.read-landing = splice.heads[operand-payload(consumer.operands[read.operands.end - 1])]
. produced = fused.ir
. mark = open-splices
. made = open-splice(produced)
made.depth = splice.depth
made.level = fused.level
made.fused = index
made.inlined = true
for argument in fused.arguments
    made.arguments += argument
made.numbers = output.numbers.length as U32
for number in produced.numbers
    output.numbers.append(number)
made.constants = output.constants.length as U32
for constant in produced.constants
    output.adopt-constant(constant)
made.locals = output.locals.length as U32
for local in produced.locals
    output.locals.append(local)
for dependency in produced.dependencies
    output.depend(dependency.kind, dependency.symbol, dependency.flags)
for _ in 0 .. < produced.blocks.length
    . reserved = output.reserve-block()
    made.heads += reserved
    made.tails += reserved
. maker-home = home(fused.maker)
made.module = if maker-home != home(output.function) then maker-home else U32.max
for id in 0 .. < produced.instructions.length
    fused.spills += if fused.crossing[id] then output.add-local(produced.instructions[id].layout) else no-local
for block in 0 .. < produced.blocks.length
    made.only += fused.body[block]
fused.depth = made.depth
fused.numbers = made.numbers
fused.constants = made.constants
fused.locals = made.locals
fused.module = made.module
for yielded in fused.yields
    . yielding = produced.instructions[yielded]
    fused.resumes += made.heads[operand-payload(produced.operands[yielding.operands.start + 1])]
    fused.closings += yielding.aux
jump(made.heads[produced.order[0]])
active += fused.maker
copy-blocks(made)
active.pop()
open-splices = mark
output.start-block(output.reserve-block())

────────────────────
_ do fuse-read
    - splice Splice
    - id ValueId
    - row IRInstruction
    - index U32

. fused = fusions[index]
if fused.resumes.length == 0
    jump(fused.after-read)
else if fused.resumes.length == 1
    jump(fused.resumes[0])
else
    . step = load-local(fused.state)
    for position in 0 .. < fused.resumes.length - 1
        . next = output.reserve-block()
        branch
            - equal(step, number(.machine-u32, (position + 1) as U64))
            - fused.resumes[position]
            - next
        output.start-block(next)
    jump(fused.resumes[fused.resumes.length - 1])
output.start-block(fused.after-read)
if row.op == .op-call
    splice.values[id] = if fused.held == no-local then fused.result else load-local(fused.held)

────────────────────
_ do fuse-end
    - splice Splice
    - id ValueId
    - row IRInstruction
    - index U32

. fused = fusions[index]
if row.op == .op-call
    splice.values[id] = blank(row.layout)
if !fused.closes
    =
. exit = output.reserve-block()
. failed = if (row.aux /and/ checked-call-flag) != 0 then landing-pad else no-block
    .. landing-pad = splice.heads[operand-payload(splice.source.operands[row.operands.end - 1])]
. step = load-local(fused.state)
store-local(fused.state, number(.machine-u32, 0))
. mark = open-splices
. closers [Splice]
for position in 0 .. < fused.closings.length
    . head = fused.closings[position]
    if head == no-block
        continue
    . closer = closing-copy(fused, index, head, exit, failed)
    . next = output.reserve-block()
    branch(equal(step, number(.machine-u32, (position + 1) as U64)), closer.heads[head], next)
    output.start-block(next)
    closers += closer
jump(exit)
active += fused.maker
for closer in closers
    copy-blocks(closer)
active.pop()
open-splices = mark
output.start-block(exit)

────────────────────
_ do closing-copy Splice
    - fused Fused
    - index U32
    - head IRBlockId
    - exit IRBlockId
    - failed IRBlockId

. produced = fused.ir
. closer = open-splice(produced)
closer.depth = fused.depth
closer.level = fused.level
closer.fused = index
closer.inlined = true
closer.closing = true
closer.exit = exit
closer.failed = failed
closer.numbers = fused.numbers
closer.constants = fused.constants
closer.locals = fused.locals
closer.module = fused.module
for argument in fused.arguments
    closer.arguments += argument
closer.only = region(produced, head)
for _ in 0 .. < produced.blocks.length
    . reserved = output.reserve-block()
    closer.heads += reserved
    closer.tails += reserved
= closer

────────────────────
_ do fused-yield
    - splice Splice
    - id ValueId
    - row IRInstruction

. fused = fusions[splice.fused]
. value = remap(splice, splice.source.operands[row.operands.start])
if fused.held == no-local
    copy(fused.result, value, output.operand-layout(fused.result))
else
    store-local(fused.held, value)
if fused.state != no-local
    for position in 0 .. < fused.yields.length
        if fused.yields[position] == id
            store-local(fused.state, number(.machine-u32, (position + 1) as U64))
jump(fused.after-read)

────────────────────
_ do fused-return
    - splice Splice
    - row IRInstruction

. fused = fusions[splice.fused]
. panicked = row.aux == ReturnKind.return-panic
if row.aux == ReturnKind.return-error
    copy
        - fused.result
        - remap(splice, splice.source.operands[row.operands.start])
        - output.operand-layout(fused.result)
    if fused.state != no-local
        store-local(fused.state, number(.machine-u32, 0))
    jump(fused.after-read)
    =
if splice.closing
    jump(if panicked then splice.failed else splice.exit)
    =
if fused.state != no-local
    store-local(fused.state, number(.machine-u32, 0))
jump(if panicked then fused.read-landing else fused.exhausted)

────────────────────
_ do copy-row
    - splice Splice
    - id ValueId
    - row IRInstruction

if row.op == .op-return && splice.continuation != no-block
    leave(splice, row)
    =
. start U32 = output.operands.length
for position in row.operands.start .. < row.operands.end
    . operand = splice.source.operands[position]
    if row.op != .op-phi
        output.add-operand(remap(splice, operand))
        continue
    if (position - row.operands.start) % 2 == 0
        splice.phi-values += output.operands.length
    else
        splice.phi-blocks += output.operands.length
    output.add-operand(operand)
. aux = row.aux
if row.op == .op-load-local || row.op == .op-store-local || row.op == .op-local-address
    aux += splice.locals
if row.op == .op-inlined-name && (splice.inlined || is-expanded(output.operands[start]))
    aux = 1
if is-call && (row.aux /and/ callee-kind-mask) == CalleeKind.callee-value
    . callee = output.operands[start]
    if operand-kind(callee) == .operand-symbol
        . position = function-of(operand-payload(callee))
        if position != no-function
            aux = row.aux - (row.aux /and/ callee-kind-mask)
            output.depend
                - .callee-function
                - position
                - if tables.functions[position].may-panic then may-panic-dependency else 0
.. is-call = row.op == .op-call || row.op == .op-call-void
. module = if row.module == U32.max then splice.module else row.module
. line = row.line
. column = row.column
if splice.inlined && splice.site-line != 0 && (row.op == .op-call || row.op == .op-call-void)
    line = splice.site-line
    column = splice.site-column
    module = splice.site-module
. operands = Span(start, output.operands.length - start)
. made = output.append
    - IRInstruction
        - row.op
        - output.current
        - row.layout
        - row.type
        - row.syntax
        - line
        - column
        - operands
        - aux
        - module
splice.values[id] = make-operand(.operand-value, made)
if splice.inlined && row.op == .op-load
    expanded-loads += made
if (row.op == .op-call || row.op == .op-call-void) && carries-notes
    carry-notes(splice, id, made, row.syntax, module)
.. carries-notes = splice.inlined || splice.source.notes.length != 0

────────────────────
_ do carry-notes
    - splice Splice
    - id ValueId
    - made ValueId
    - syntax SyntaxId
    - module ModuleId

. copy = output.instructions[made]
. kind = copy.aux /and/ callee-kind-mask
. target = no-function
if kind == CalleeKind.callee-function && operand-kind(callee) == .operand-symbol
    target = function-of(operand-payload(output.operands[copy.operands.start]))
.. callee = output.operands[copy.operands.start]
. site-module = placed(if splice.inlined then splice.site-module else module, output.function)
. site-syntax = if splice.inlined then splice.site-syntax else syntax
. noted = false
for note in splice.source.notes
    if note.row == id && (kind == CalleeKind.callee-value || note.target == target)
        noted = true
        if splice.inlined
            output.note(made, note.target, site-module, site-syntax, chained(note.chain))
        else
            output.note(made, note.target, note.site-module, note.site-syntax, note.chain)
if splice.inlined && !noted && target != no-function && falls-back(target)
    output.note(made, target, site-module, site-syntax, chained(IdList()))

────────────────────
_ placed ModuleId
    - module ModuleId
    - function FunctionId

if module != U32.max then module else home(function)

────────────────────
_ do chained IdList
    - chain IdList

. made = IdList()
for position in 1 .. < active.length
    made = output.extended(made, active[position])
for position in 0 .. < chain.length
    made = output.extended(made, chain[position])
= made

────────────────────
+ do warnings String
    - ir IRFunction

if program.is-batch
    = ""
. targets [FunctionId]
. reasons [Bool]
. modules [ModuleId]
. syntaxes [SyntaxId]
. chains [IdList]
for position in 0 .. < ir.order.length
    . rows = ir.blocks[ir.order[position]].instructions
    for id in rows.start .. < rows.end
        . row = ir.instructions[id]
        if row.op != .op-call && row.op != .op-call-void
            continue
        . kind = row.aux /and/ callee-kind-mask
        . target = no-function
        if kind == CalleeKind.callee-function && operand-kind(callee) == .operand-symbol
            target = function-of(operand-payload(ir.operands[row.operands.start]))
            if target != no-function && !falls-back(target)
                target = no-function
        .. callee = ir.operands[row.operands.start]
        . module = placed(row.module, ir.function)
        . syntax = row.syntax
        . chain = IdList()
        for note in ir.notes
            if note.row == id && (kind == CalleeKind.callee-value || note.target == target)
                target = note.target
                module = note.site-module
                syntax = note.site-syntax
                chain = note.chain
        if target == no-function || module != program.entry-module
            continue
        . recursive = kind == CalleeKind.callee-function
        . found = U32.max
        for index in 0 .. < targets.length
            if targets[index] == target && reasons[index] == recursive && same-site
                found = index as U32
            .. same-site = modules[index] == module && syntaxes[index] == syntax
        if found == U32.max
            targets += target
            reasons += recursive
            modules += module
            syntaxes += syntax
            chains += chain
        else if chains[found].length == 0
            chains[found] = chain
. sources = use ExcerptSources(program)
= "\n".join(warning-text(targets[each], reasons[each], modules[each], syntaxes[each], chains[each], sources) in 0 .. < targets.length)

────────────────────
_ do warning-text String
    - target FunctionId
    - recursive Bool
    - module ModuleId
    - syntax SyntaxId
    - chain IdList
    - sources ExcerptSources

. loc = program.modules[module].tree.nodes[syntax].loc
. site = "${module-path(module)}:${loc.begin.line + 1}"
. reason = if recursive then "recursive function" else "unresolved target: virtual dispatch"
. row = instances.rows[tables.functions[target].instance]
. message = "Cannot inline ${display(target)}: $reason; @inline declaration at $path:$line"
    .. path = module-path(row.module)
    .. line = declared-line(target)
if chain.length != 0
    . steps [String]
    for position in 0 .. < chain.length
        steps += "${display(chain[position])} at $site"
    message = "$message; expanded through ${" -> ".join(steps)}"
= "Warning: $message\n<$site>\n${sources.excerpt(module, loc)}"

────────────────────
_ display String
    - position FunctionId

tables.bundle.text(tables.functions[position].display)

────────────────────
_ module-path String
    - module ModuleId

if path.size != 0 then path else "no file"

.. path = program.modules[module].path

────────────────────
_ do declared-line U32
    - position FunctionId

. row = instances.rows[tables.functions[position].instance]
. tree = program.modules[row.module].tree
match? program.modules[row.module].decls[row.decl]
    | .decl-function(fn)
        = tree.nodes[fn.syntax].loc.begin.line + 1
    | .decl-converter(converter)
        = tree.nodes[converter.syntax].loc.begin.line + 1
= 0

────────────────────
_ is-expanded Bool
    - operand Operand

operand-kind(operand) == .operand-value && expanded-loads.find(operand-payload(operand)) != null

────────────────────
_ do remap Operand
    - splice Splice
    - operand Operand

. payload = operand-payload(operand)
if operand-kind(operand) == .operand-value && spilled && crosses-block
    = load-local(fusions[splice.fused].spills[payload])
.. spilled = splice.fused != U32.max && fusions[splice.fused].spills[payload] != no-local
.. crosses-block = splice.source.instructions[payload].block != splice.block
= match operand-kind(operand)
    |= .operand-value
        splice.values[payload]
    |= .operand-argument
        if splice.inlined then splice.arguments[payload] else operand
    |= .operand-number
        make-operand(.operand-number, payload + splice.numbers)
    |= .operand-constant
        make-operand(.operand-constant, payload + splice.constants)
    |= .operand-block
        make-operand(.operand-block, splice.heads[payload])
    |= .operand-result
        if splice.continuation != no-block then splice.result else operand
    ??
        operand

────────────────────
_ do leave
    - splice Splice
    - row IRInstruction

if row.aux == ReturnKind.return-panic
    jump(splice.landing)
    =
if row.operands.count != 0
    . value = remap(splice, splice.source.operands[row.operands.start])
    if tables.layouts.is-struct(splice.source.returns)
        if splice.result != 0 && value != splice.result
            copy(splice.result, value, splice.source.returns)
    else
        splice.returned += value
        splice.arrived += output.current
jump(splice.continuation)

────────────────────
_ do expand Bool
    - splice Splice
    - id ValueId
    - row IRInstruction
    - callee FunctionId

if splice.depth >= inline-depth || active.find(callee) != null
    = false
. asked = requested(callee)
. reading = !asked && reads-tuple(callee)
. small = !asked && !reading
. found = emitted(callee)
if !found
    = false
. inlined = found
. checked = (row.aux /and/ checked-call-flag) != 0
. last = row.operands.end - (if checked then 1u32 else 0u32)
. given = last - row.operands.start - 1
if inlined.arguments.length != given || !fits(inlined, checked, row)
    = false
. mark = open-splices
. made = open-splice(inlined)
made.depth = splice.depth + 1
made.inlined = true
made.small = small
made.site-line = if splice.inlined then splice.site-line else row.line
made.site-column = if splice.inlined then splice.site-column else row.column
made.site-module = if splice.inlined then splice.site-module else row.module
made.site-syntax = if splice.inlined then splice.site-syntax else row.syntax
made.numbers = output.numbers.length as U32
for number in inlined.numbers
    output.numbers.append(number)
made.constants = output.constants.length as U32
for constant in inlined.constants
    output.adopt-constant(constant)
made.locals = output.locals.length as U32
for local in inlined.locals
    output.locals.append(local)
for dependency in inlined.dependencies
    output.depend(dependency.kind, dependency.symbol, dependency.flags)
for _ in 0 .. < inlined.blocks.length
    . reserved = output.reserve-block()
    made.heads += reserved
    made.tails += reserved
. callee-home = home(callee)
made.module = if callee-home != home(output.function) then callee-home else U32.max
if checked
    made.landing = splice.heads[operand-payload(splice.source.operands[row.operands.end - 1])]
made.continuation = output.reserve-block()
for position in 0 .. < given
    . operand = remap(splice, splice.source.operands[row.operands.start + 1 + position])
    . layout = inlined.arguments[position]
    if tables.layouts.is-struct(layout) && tables.layouts.rows[layout].size != 0 && !reading
        . held = frame(layout)
        copy(held, operand, layout)
        made.arguments += held
    else
        made.arguments += operand
. structured = row.op == .op-call && tables.layouts.is-struct(row.layout)
. returned = if structured then returned-frame(inlined) else U32.max
if structured && returned == U32.max
    made.result = frame(row.layout)
jump(made.heads[inlined.order[0]])
active += callee
copy-blocks(made)
active.pop()
grew = true
expanded = true
output.start-block(made.continuation)
if row.op == .op-call
    if structured
        splice.values[id] = if returned == U32.max then made.result else made.values[returned]
    else if made.returned.length == 0
        splice.values[id] = blank(row.layout)
    else if made.returned.length == 1
        splice.values[id] = made.returned[0]
    else
        splice.values[id] = phi-of(row, made.returned, made.arrived)
open-splices = mark
= true

────────────────────
_ do expands-any Bool
    - inlined IRFunction

` Whether a body calls a function that is inlined wherever it is called, or names the
` environment of a closure, either of which a body inlined as a small one would have to expand
` in turn, or asks for a name that is another where it is inlined.
for made in inlined.instructions
    if made.op == .op-inlined-name
        = true
    if made.op == .op-call || made.op == .op-call-void
        . target = inlined.operands[made.operands.start]
        . position = if is-symbol then function-of(operand-payload(target)) else no-function
            .. is-symbol = operand-kind(target) == .operand-symbol
        if position != no-function && (requested(position) || signs-reader(position))
            = true
    for index in made.operands.start .. < made.operands.end
        if operand-kind(inlined.operands[index]) == .operand-environment
            = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do returned-frame U32
    - ir IRFunction

` The frame a function returns where it returns from one place, which the call it is inlined
` for gives as its value in place of a copy. None where it returns from more, or leaves its
` value where its caller asked.
. found = U32.max
for row in ir.instructions
    if row.op == .op-return && row.aux != ReturnKind.return-panic
        if found != U32.max || row.operands.count == 0
            = U32.max
        . value = ir.operands[row.operands.start]
        if not-value || ir.instructions[operand-payload(value)].op != .op-frame
            = U32.max
        .. not-value = operand-kind(value) != .operand-value
        found = operand-payload(value)
for position in 0 .. < ir.operands.length
    if operand-kind(ir.operands[position]) == .operand-result
        = U32.max
= found

────────────────────
_ do fits Bool
    - inlined IRFunction
    - checked Bool
    - row IRInstruction

if inlined.order.length == 0 || (inlined.signals && !checked)
    = false
if row.op == .op-call
    if inlined.returns != row.layout
        = false
    if tables.layouts.is-struct(row.layout) && tables.layouts.rows[row.layout].size == 0
        = false
. returns = false
for made in inlined.instructions
    if made.op == .op-return
        if made.aux == ReturnKind.return-panic
            if !checked
                = false
        else
            returns = true
    for position in made.operands.start .. < made.operands.end
        if operand-kind(inlined.operands[position]) == .operand-environment
            = false
= returns

────────────────────
_ do blank Operand
    - layout LayoutId

if layout == void-layout
    = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
if tables.layouts.is-struct(layout)
    . made = frame(layout)
    zero(made, layout)
    = made
= number(layout as MachineKind, 0)

────────────────────
_ do number Operand
    - kind MachineKind
    - bits U64

= make-operand(.operand-number, output.add-number(kind, bits))

────────────────────
_ do frame Operand
    - layout LayoutId

= make-operand
    - .operand-value
    - output.append
        - IRInstruction(.op-frame, output.current, layout, no-type, 0, 0, 0, Span(), layout)

────────────────────
_ do zero
    - target Operand
    - layout LayoutId

. start U32 = output.operands.length
output.add-operand(target)
output.append
    - IRInstruction(.op-zero, output.current, void-layout, no-type, 0, 0, 0, Span(start, 1), layout)

────────────────────
_ do load-local Operand
    - local LocalId

= make-operand
    - .operand-value
    - output.append
        - IRInstruction
            - .op-load-local
            - output.current
            - output.locals[local].layout
            - no-type
            - 0
            - 0
            - 0
            - Span()
            - local

────────────────────
_ do store-local
    - local LocalId
    - value Operand

. start U32 = output.operands.length
output.add-operand(value)
output.append
    - IRInstruction
        - .op-store-local
        - output.current
        - void-layout
        - no-type
        - 0
        - 0
        - 0
        - Span(start, 1)
        - local

────────────────────
_ do equal Operand
    - left Operand
    - right Operand

. start U32 = output.operands.length
output.add-operand(left)
output.add-operand(right)
= make-operand
    - .operand-value
    - output.append
        - IRInstruction
            - .op-compare
            - output.current
            - u8-layout
            - no-type
            - 0
            - 0
            - 0
            - Span(start, 2)
            - ComparePredicate.compare-equal

────────────────────
_ do copy
    - target Operand
    - source Operand
    - layout LayoutId

. start U32 = output.operands.length
output.add-operand(target)
output.add-operand(source)
output.append
    - IRInstruction(.op-copy, output.current, void-layout, no-type, 0, 0, 0, Span(start, 2), layout)

────────────────────
_ do jump
    - target IRBlockId

. start U32 = output.operands.length
output.add-operand(make-operand(.operand-block, target))
output.append
    - IRInstruction(.op-jump, output.current, void-layout, no-type, 0, 0, 0, Span(start, 1), 0)

────────────────────
_ do branch
    - condition Operand
    - taken IRBlockId
    - other IRBlockId

. start U32 = output.operands.length
output.add-operand(condition)
output.add-operand(make-operand(.operand-block, taken))
output.add-operand(make-operand(.operand-block, other))
output.append
    - IRInstruction(.op-branch, output.current, void-layout, no-type, 0, 0, 0, Span(start, 3), 0)

────────────────────
_ do phi-of Operand
    - row IRInstruction
    - values [Operand]
    - blocks [IRBlockId]

. start U32 = output.operands.length
for position in 0 .. < values.length
    output.add-operand(values[position])
    output.add-operand(make-operand(.operand-block, blocks[position]))
. operands = Span(start, output.operands.length - start)
= make-operand
    - .operand-value
    - output.append
        - IRInstruction(.op-phi, output.current, row.layout, row.type, 0, 0, 0, operands, 0)
